"""Original contextual morphology and suffix generalisation questions."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
items=[]
def add(b,q,c,w,why):
 n=sum(x['bank']==b for x in items)+1;p=(n-1)%4;o=w.split('~');o.insert(p,c)
 items.append(dict(id=f'AC9E3LY10-{b[0].upper()}-{n:03d}',subject='english',year_level='Year 3',curriculum_code='AC9E3LY10',bank=b,skill='Use word parts to understand new words',question=q,audio_prompt=q,visual={'type':'none'},answers=[{'text':s,'is_correct':j==p} for j,s in enumerate(o)],correct_index=p,explanation={'summary':why,'hint':'Find a meaningful base and affix, then check how the whole word fits the sentence.'}))
p='''We will rebuild the fallen tower. What does rebuild tell you?|Build it again.|Build it badly.~Build it before it exists.~Never build it.|Re- means again; rebuild means build again.
The food was precooked before it reached the kitchen. What does pre- add?|The cooking happened beforehand.|The food was cooked incorrectly.~The food had no cooking.~The cooking happened twice.|Pre- means before; precooked means cooked beforehand.
The label was misprinted, so the name had the wrong letter. What does misprinted mean?|Printed incorrectly.|Printed again correctly.~Printed before lunch.~Not printed at all.|Mis- signals an incorrect result; the wrong letter supports that meaning.
The knot was untied before the ribbon was used again. What happened?|Someone reversed the tying.|Someone tied it twice.~Someone made it brighter.~Someone cut every ribbon.|Un- can reverse an action; untied means the tying was undone, not necessarily that anything was cut.
An unhappy ending leaves the character feeling sad. What does un- mean here?|Not.|Again.~Before.~Full of.|Unhappy means not happy; here un- expresses the opposite rather than reversing an action.
A fearless firefighter stayed calm in the story. What does -less add to fear?|Without fear.|Full of fear.~Fear again.~Able to make fear.|-Less means without; the word describes lacking fear.
The helpful sign showed us the correct entrance. What does helpful mean?|Giving help.|Without help.~Needing help again.~Unable to help.|Help is the base; -ful forms an adjective describing something that gives help in this context.
The cup is washable. Which explanation fits?|It can be washed.|It has already been washed twice.~It must never be washed.~It washes other cups.|-Able means able to be; washable describes something that can be washed.
The agreement said both teams could use the oval. What is an agreement?|A result of agreeing.|Someone unable to agree.~Agreeing incorrectly.~A place with no teams.|Agree plus -ment names an action or result; here it is what the teams agreed.
The child spoke softly beside the sleeping baby. What does softly describe?|Speaking in a soft way.|A state of being soft.~A person who is soft.~Speaking again.|Soft plus -ly describes the manner of speaking.
Her kindness made the new pupil feel welcome. What does kindness name?|The quality of being kind.|Acting in a quick way.~A person called Kind.~Being kind before lunch only.|-Ness turns kind into the name of a quality or state.
The bags were reusable, so we kept them. Which parts explain reusable?|Re- means again; use is the base; -able means able to be.|Re- means wrong; usable means broken.~Reuse means throw away; -able means without.~Re- means before; -able means a person.|Reusable means able to be used again; both affixes contribute to the meaning.
Which word is the base in careless, as in a careless mistake?|care|car~less~carelessy|Care can stand alone and carries the central meaning; -less adds without.
Which word is the base in disagreement?|agree|dis~ment~greement|Dis- and -ment surround the base agree; disagreement means a difference or lack of agreement.
Which explanation avoids a false word split? The word reply appears in a letter.|Do not treat ply as its everyday base meaning here.|Reply means ply again in this sentence.~Every word starting re must mean again.~Remove re from every long word.|Not every initial re is a useful re- prefix in everyday word analysis; check a meaningful base and whole-word meaning.
The class will preview the film clip before choosing it. What will they do?|View it beforehand.|View it badly.~Refuse to view it.~View every film ever made.|Pre- adds before to view; the sentence confirms an advance viewing.
The painter repainted the door. What does the word tell us for certain?|The door was painted again.|The new paint was blue.~The door was broken.~The painter used a roller.|Re- supports again; it does not reveal colour, damage or tools.
The garden was colourless in the black-and-white drawing. What does colourless mean here?|Without colour.|Full of every colour.~Able to colour things.~Colouring again.|Colour plus -less means without colour; the drawing context confirms this.
A hopeful player expected the team to improve. Which word names that quality?|hopefulness|hopelessness~hopelessly~replay|Hopeful plus -ness names the quality of being hopeful; hopelessness has the opposite meaning.
The box was moved carefully. Which explanation uses both word parts?|Careful means taking care; -ly tells how it was moved.|Care is a place; fully means again.~-Ly means without care.~Carefully means it was never moved.|Carefully describes the manner of moving, with care.
The puppy chased one ball. Now it chases two ___. Which form and rule fit?|balls: add s to ball.|balles: add es to every noun.~ballies: change ll to ies.~ball: plurals never change.|The regular plural of ball is balls; this base takes s.
One brush is dry; three ___ are wet. Choose the correct formation.|brushes: add es after sh.|brushs: always add only s.~brushies: add ies after every h.~brushe: remove the final s.|Brush ends in sh, so its regular plural adds es.
One berry fell; several ___ remained. Which rule gives the plural?|berries: after a consonant, change only final y to i and add es.|berrys: keep y after every consonant.~berris: remove y and add is.~berres: remove both r and y.|Berry ends with a consonant before y; change y to i and add es.
One toy broke; the other ___ were safe. Why is toys correct?|A vowel comes before y, so keep y and add s.|Every y changes to ies.~The y is removed before s.~Toy is always singular.|Toy has vowel o before y, so the regular plural keeps y.
The children were hoping for rain. Which base and change make hoping?|Hope: drop final e before ing.|Hop: add ing without doubling.~Hoping: add another ing.~Hope: keep e before ing.|Hope loses its silent final e before ing; hoping means having hope, not jumping.
The rabbit was hopping. Why are there two p letters?|Hop has one short vowel before final p; double p before ing.|Every word doubles its last letter before ing.~Hoping and hopping have identical meanings.~The base already ends in pp.|The one-syllable base hop doubles p before ing, keeping the short-vowel pattern distinct from hope/hoping.
The team tried again. Which formation is correct?|try → tried: after a consonant, change only final y to i, then add ed.|try → tryed: always keep y.~try → triid: add id.~try → treed: change the vowel to ee.|Try ends consonant + y; tried is its regular past form.
The children played outside. Why does played keep y?|Play has a vowel before y, so add ed without changing y.|All y words must keep y.~Played is a plural noun.~The y is a suffix.|Play ends vowel + y; its past form is played.
The box is movable. Which base has changed?|Move loses final e before able.|Mov is an independent base word.~Move loses m before able.~Able changes to ible in movable.|Movable is move plus able, with final e removed; it means able to be moved.
The path was muddy. Which base helps explain muddy?|Mud: having or covered with mud.|Muddy: a path with no mud.~Mood: feeling sad.~My: belonging to someone.|Mud is the base; adding y forms muddy, with d doubled.
The room became darker after sunset. What does -er mean here?|More dark.|A person who darks.~Without darkness.~Dark again.|In darker, -er compares the quality dark; it does not name a worker.
A baker made bread. What does -er mean here?|A person who bakes.|More baked than before.~Without baking.~Baking incorrectly.|Bake plus -er names the person; its final e is not written twice.
The class chose the smallest seed from the three. What does -est show?|The seed has the least size in this group.|Someone who makes seeds.~A seed planted again.~A seed with no size at all.|Smallest compares more than two and identifies the one furthest towards small within the stated group.
The two boxes looked identical, but this one is heavier. What base meaning remains in heavier?|Heavy: having more weight.|Heave: throwing something.~Hear: listening closely.~Every: all of them.|Heavier is heavy plus er, with y changed to i. It means more heavy; identical appearance need not mean equal weight.
The sign said PAYMENT DUE. Which verb helps explain payment?|pay|paint~play~point|Pay plus ment names the action or result of paying.
Their friendship lasted for years. Which base helps explain the relationship?|friend|ship~end~fresh|Friend is the base; friendship names the relationship of being friends, not a boat.
The bicycle was unlocked, so the rider could use it. What action does unlocked describe?|The locking was reversed.|The bicycle was made unsafe forever.~The lock was bought twice.~The bicycle became smaller.|Un- reverses lock here; the word does not establish every other condition of the bicycle.
The gardener overwatered the plant. What does over- add?|Too much watering.|Watering before planting only.~No watering at all.~Watering correctly once.|Over- can mean too much; overwatered means given too much water.
The soup was undercooked. Which meaning fits?|It had not been cooked enough.|It was always cooked underground.~It had been cooked too much.~It was cooked again.|Under- means insufficiently here; the whole word concerns how much cooking it received.
A listener heard the announcement. Which word part names the person?|The ending er added to listen.|The beginning list means person.~The final r means again.~The whole word means a loud sound.|Listen plus er names someone who listens.
The child moved fearlessly across the stage. Which meaning fits all the parts?|In a way showing no fear.|In a way full of fear.~A state of being afraid.~A person who causes fear.|Fear + less + ly combines without fear and manner of acting.
The instructions were unclear. What does unclear tell the reader?|They were not clear.|They were clear again.~They had been read twice.~They were written in another country.|Un- negates clear; it does not tell us the language or reading history.
The shop sells musical toys. How does music help explain musical?|The toys are connected with music.|The toys have no music.~The toys are all musicians.~The toys were bought again.|Music is the base; musical means relating to music, not necessarily a person who performs.
The runner stopped beside the gate. Which formation is correct?|stop + ed → stopped|stop + ed → stoped~stop + ed → stopied~stop + ed → stope|The one-syllable short-vowel base stop doubles final p before ed.
The birds were singing. Why is sing not changed to singg before ing?|The base ends in two consonant letters, ng; add ing.|Every final consonant is doubled.~The word has no vowel.~The base is sin and g is removed.|Sing keeps its existing ng ending and adds ing; do not apply the single-final-consonant doubling pattern here.
The child was crying. Why does crying keep y?|Keep y when adding ing to cry.|Change every y to i before ing.~The base is crie.~The word has no suffix.|Cry keeps y before ing; the y-to-i change used in cried is not applied here.
The story was enjoyable. Which parts explain the word?|Enjoy + able: able to be enjoyed.|En + joyable: a person who writes.~Enjoy + less: without enjoyment.~Re + enjoy: enjoyed again only.|Enjoyable uses enjoy with able; in context it describes a story that can be enjoyed.
The plan needs improvement. What does improvement mean?|The action or result of making it better.|A person who improves plans.~A plan that cannot improve.~Improving before anything happens only.|Improve plus ment names an action or result; improvement retains the e of improve before ment.'''
for row in p.splitlines():add('practice',*row.split('|'))
t='''We must reread the message because we missed a detail. What does reread mean?|Read again.|Read incorrectly.~Read before it is written.~Stop reading forever.|Re- adds again; the reason in the sentence supports another reading.
The parcel was prepaid. What does prepaid mean?|Paid for beforehand.|Paid for incorrectly.~Never paid for.~Paid for twice in every case.|Pre- means before; prepaid does not necessarily mean a second payment.
A careless reader misread the number. Which meaning fits misread?|Read it incorrectly.|Read it again accurately.~Read it beforehand.~Refused to read it.|Mis- changes read to an incorrect reading.
The jacket is waterproof, but it is not weightless. What does weightless mean?|Without weight.|Full of water.~Able to be weighed again.~Heavier than all jackets.|Weight plus less means without weight; the sentence says this jacket is not weightless.
The child answered politely. What does -ly contribute?|It describes the way the child answered.|It names a group of children.~It means not polite.~It means answering beforehand.|Politely uses ly to express manner: in a polite way.
The darkness made the room hard to see. What does darkness name?|The state of being dark.|A person who darkens rooms.~A way of speaking loudly.~Something that can be darkened again.|Dark plus ness names a state or quality.
The glass is breakable. Which explanation fits the suffix?|It is able to be broken.|It has already broken twice.~It cannot break.~It breaks other objects.|Able adds the possibility of being broken; it does not say the glass is already broken.
One city has a station; several ___ have stations. Which form is correct?|cities|citys~citis~cityes|City ends consonant + y; change y to i and add es.
The dog is wagging its tail. Which base and rule explain the spelling?|Wag: double g before ing after its short vowel.|Wage: keep e and add ing.~Wag: remove g before ing.~Wagging: add another g to every word.|The one-syllable base wag doubles its final g before ing.
The artist was smiling. Which base gives this form?|Smile, with final e dropped before ing.|Smil, with no change.~Smell, with e changed to i.~Smiling, with ing added twice.|Smile loses final e before ing; it remains connected to the action smile.
We carried the boxes inside. Which change produces carried?|Carry: after a consonant, change only final y to i and add ed.|Carry: add d only.~Carry: change rr to r and add ed.~Care: add ried.|Carry forms carried by changing y to i before ed.
The games were replayed after a technical problem. Which meaning uses both affixes?|Played again, with ed marking the past action.|Played incorrectly in the future.~Never played at all.~People who play games.|Re- adds again and ed gives the past form of play; the base keeps y.
The writer described a peaceful lake. How does peace help explain peaceful?|The lake is described as having peace or calm.|The lake has no peace.~The lake can write stories.~The lake was visited again.|Peace plus ful forms peaceful; the adjective describes calm in this context.
The younger child spoke first. What does -er mean in younger?|More young compared with another person.|A person whose job is younging.~Without youth.~Young again after being old.|Younger compares age; er here is comparative, not a worker suffix.
The repair was successful. What does the ending ful help show?|The repair achieved success.|The repair had no success.~The repair must happen again.~The repair was impossible.|Successful is connected to success; the whole word means achieving the intended result.
The chef tasted the soup. Why does tasted have only one e before d?|Taste already ends in e, so add d.|All past words lose their final vowel.~The base is tast and ed is never added.~Taste doubles its t and e.|For taste, the regular past is formed by adding d to the existing final e.'''
for row in t.splitlines():add('test',*row.split('|'))
assert len(items)==64,len(items)
assert sum(x['bank']=='practice' for x in items)==48
# Actual formation complements contextual recognition; targets are not printed in prompts.
formation={
('practice',1):('The tower fell and will be built again.','build','re-','Write the new word, then use it in a sentence about the tower. Explain what the prefix adds.','rebuild; re- means again. Accept a sentence describing building the tower again.'),
('practice',2):('The kitchen needs food cooked beforehand.','cook','pre- and -ed','Form one word using both affixes. Write a label sentence and explain the before meaning.','precooked; cooked beforehand. Keep pre, cook and ed in order.'),
('practice',3):('The name on a poster was printed incorrectly.','print','mis- and -ed','Form the word describing the mistake, then write a sentence showing what went wrong.','misprinted; printed incorrectly. The sentence should connect the word to an incorrect printing.'),
('practice',4):('Someone reverses the action of tying a ribbon.','tie','un-','Write the new action word. Use it in an instruction and explain how un- changes tie.','untie; reverse the tying. An instruction such as Untie the ribbon is suitable.'),
('practice',5):('A story character is not happy with the ending.','happy','un-','Form the describing word and write a sentence about the character. Explain the meaning of un- here.','unhappy; not happy. The base spelling remains happy, unlike suffix changes to happiness.'),
('practice',6):('A fictional explorer shows no fear.','fear','-less','Write the describing word. Use it in a sentence and explain the meaning added by the suffix.','fearless; without fear. The sentence should use the adjective meaningfully.'),
('practice',7):('A sign gives people useful help.','help','-ful','Form the describing word, write a sentence about the sign, and explain how the word connects to help.','helpful; giving help. The suffix ful has one l.'),
('practice',8):('A fabric bag can be washed.','wash','-able','Form one word describing the bag. Write a sentence and explain the able-to-be meaning.','washable; able to be washed. No letters are removed from wash.'),
('practice',9):('Two teams agree on how to share a field.','agree','-ment','Form the noun for what they reach. Use it in a sentence and explain what the noun names.','agreement; the result of agreeing. Keep the final e of agree before ment.'),
('practice',10):('The baby is asleep, so a child speaks in a soft way.','soft','-ly','Form the word describing how the child speaks. Write the sentence and explain the suffix.','softly; in a soft way. Use it to describe the manner of speaking.'),
('practice',11):('A pupil shows the quality of being kind.','kind','-ness','Write the noun naming this quality. Use it in a sentence about welcoming someone.','kindness; the quality or state of being kind. Keep all letters in kind before adding ness.'),
('practice',12):('A bag can be used again.','use','re- and -able','Form one word using both affixes. Explain each affix and use the whole word in a sentence.','reusable; able to be used again. Standard spelling drops the e of use before able.'),
('test',1):('A message needs to be read again.','read','re-','Form the verb, use it in a sentence, and explain what the prefix adds.','reread; read again. Accept a meaningful present or past sentence with appropriate spoken pronunciation.'),
('test',2):('A parcel has been paid for beforehand.','paid','pre-','Write the new word and a sentence about the parcel. Explain the prefix meaning.','prepaid; paid beforehand. The spelling keeps paid after pre.'),
('test',3):('A number was read incorrectly.','read','mis-','Form the verb and use it in a sentence explaining the error. Explain the prefix meaning.','misread; read incorrectly. Accept suitable present or past use; the spelling stays read.'),
('test',4):('In a fantasy story, an object has no weight.','weight','-less','Form the adjective and write a sentence using it. Explain the suffix meaning.','weightless; without weight. Retain the complete base weight before less.')}
for x in items:
 k=(x['bank'],int(x['id'].rsplit('-',1)[1]))
 if k not in formation:continue
 context,baseword,affixes,task,model=formation[k]
 q=f'{context}\n\nBase: {baseword}. Word parts to add: {affixes}. {task}'
 x.update(question=q,audio_prompt=q,grading_mode='adult-review',answers=[],correct_index=None,model_answer=model,acceptance_note='View the formed word and the learner’s own sentence, and hear or read the requested explanation. Check accurate affix/base spelling and whole-word meaning in context. Accept different sensible sentences. Do not award achievement for a completion tick alone; ask the learner to explain the parts if the written answer is unclear.',response_instructions='Write the formed word and your sentence. Read them to an adult and give the explanation requested in the task. An adult will check the response.',completion_label='I have formed and explained the word; an adult still needs to check.',explanation={'summary':model,'hint':'Join the meaningful parts carefully. Check whether the base spelling changes, then test the whole word in your sentence.'})
Path(__file__).with_name('ac9e3ly10.json').write_text(json.dumps(items,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
